Notebook[{Cell["Transversely polarized proton-proton classes (A_TT), step 3: \
scalar integrals", "Title"], Cell["Input: \
Results/<route>/class-<n>/Algebra.wl (step 2).  Output: \
Results/<route>/class-<n>/Reduced.wl with the real-emission phase-space \
integrals and the one-loop integrals evaluated as Laurent series in eps, \
exact in the threshold variable, for the two spin projections of step 2: \
\"TT\" (the hard part of A_TT) and \"Symmetric\" (the evanescent \
Phi-independent part, carried along as a check).  This file is that of \
Processes/Hadronic/3-Reduce.wl (read its introduction for the method: partial \
fractions into the six cut families, Kira reduction with the families of \
kira/, the phase-space and loop masters, the continuation to the physical \
region); the integrands of step 2 are rational functions of the same \
invariants, with the same hatted invariant spe3 and hat powers of the loop \
momentum, so nothing changes in the reduction.  The normal components of the \
unobserved and loop momenta were already reduced to invariants in step \
2.\n\nReal emission.  The two unobserved partons k1, k2 (k1 + k2 = pRec = pa \
+ pb - p, pRec^2 = s4 = s + t + u) are integrated with the two-body phase \
space written as cut propagators k1^2 and k2^2.  Every denominator of the \
squared matrix element is a linear form in the two independent invariants A = \
(k1-pa)^2 and B = (k1-pb)^2: besides A and B these are C = (k1+p)^2 = -s4 - A \
- B and, with k2, A' = (k2-pa)^2 = -(s+t) - A, B' = (k2-pb)^2 = -(s+u) - B, \
C' = (k2+p)^2 = s + A + B.  Any three of them are linearly dependent (two \
variables), so partial fractions reduce every term to at most two forms, and \
the exchange k1 <-> k2 (a symmetry of the phase space) maps the primed pairs \
onto unprimed ones.  Six families remain, defined in \
kira/real/config/integralfamilies.yaml:\n\n   real_AB[1,1,n3,n4] = integral \
of 1/(A^n3 B^n4),  real_AC, real_BC, real_ABp (A and B'), real_ACp (A and \
C'), real_BCp (B and C').\n\nKira reduces them to the two-body volume and one \
angular master per family.  The angular master of two massless \"legs\" q, q' \
(the external momenta of the two forms) depends on the angle between them in \
the rest frame of pRec; with z = s4 (q.q')/(2 (q.pRec)(q'.pRec)) for two \
forms with the same unobserved momentum, and 1 - z when one form has k1 and \
the other k2,\n\n   integral of 1/(X Y) over the phase space = sigmaX sigmaY \
Phi2 Omega(z)/((2 q.pRec)(2 q'.pRec)),   sigma = -1 for A, B, A', B' (= -2 \
q.k) and +1 for C, C' (= +2 q.k),\n\nwith Omega(z) = 2(1-2eps) \
integral_0^Infinity dx x^(-1-eps)(1+x)^eps/(z+x) exactly as in the \
lepton-quark process, whose threshold branches z^(-1-eps) and regular part \
F1(z) are separated by the hypergeometric connection formula; the hatted \
invariant spe3 shifts the dimension by two for each power, with the masters \
Phi2' and Omega2.\n\nVirtual.  The one-loop families virtual_ST, virtual_SU, \
virtual_TU (massless boxes) are reduced by Kira to the bubbles in s, t, u and \
the boxes in (s,t), (s,u), (t,u).  The bubbles are Euler integrals; the boxes \
are evaluated from their Feynman-parameter representation with SubTropica in \
the Euclidean region and continued to the physical region (s > 0), where \
their real parts enter.  Powers of the hatted loop momentum loopHat2 shift \
the dimension by two (masters in D+2).", "Text"], Cell["Load", "Section"], 
  Cell["Get[FileNameJoin[{NotebookDirectory[], \"..\", \"..\", \"FeynFacet\", \
\"FeynFacet.wl\"}]]", "Input"], Cell["route = \"FeynCalc\";\nclass = \
\"5\";\nalgebra = LoadResult[\"Algebra\", route <> \"/class-\" <> \
class];\nspins = {\"TT\", \"Symmetric\"};\nKeys[algebra]", "Input"], 
  Cell["Real emission: partial fractions", "Section"], 
  Cell["The squared matrix element, with D = 4 - 2 eps, is a rational \
function of A and B (C is eliminated) with coefficients rational in eps.  Its \
denominator factors are the six linear forms, which are replaced by the inert \
symbols fA, fB, fC, fAp, fBp, fCp; then two kinds of rules are applied \
repeatedly until no term contains more than two forms: for a dependent pair \
(A A', B B', C C', whose sums are constants) 1/(L L') = (1/L + 1/L')/(L + \
L'), and for any three forms with alpha L1 + beta L2 + gamma L3 = delta \
(constants), 1/(L1 L2 L3) = [alpha/(L2 L3) + beta/(L1 L3) + gamma/(L1 \
L2)]/delta.", "Text"], Cell["forms = <|fA -> A, fB -> B, fC -> -s4 - A - B, \
fAp -> -(s + t) - A, fBp -> -(s + u) - B, fCp -> s + A + B|> /. u -> s4 - s - \
t;\nformOf[factor_] := Module[{f = Expand[factor], matches},\n  matches = \
Select[Keys[forms], Expand[f - forms[#]] === 0 || Expand[f + forms[#]] === 0 \
&];\n  Require[Length[matches] == 1, \"A denominator factor is not one of the \
six linear forms\", factor];\n  First[matches] If[Expand[f - \
forms[First[matches]]] === 0, 1, -1]];\n(* write the denominator through the \
inert form symbols; the numerator keeps A, B (they are removed below) \
*)\ntoForms[expr_] := Module[{mapped = MapIntegrationDenominators[expr,\n    \
{u -> s4 - s - t, C -> -s4 - A - B}, {A, B}, formOf]},\n  \
Require[!FailureQ[mapped], \"Termwise denominator conversion failed\", \
mapped];\n  mapped];\n(* numerators: A and B are themselves forms \
*)\nnumeratorForms = {A -> fA, B -> fB};\nrelation[names_List] := Module[{L = \
forms /@ names, al, be, ga, sol},\n  sol = Quiet[Solve[{Coefficient[al L[[1]] \
+ be L[[2]] + ga L[[3]], A] == 0, Coefficient[al L[[1]] + be L[[2]] + ga \
L[[3]], B] == 0, al == 1}, {al, be, ga}], Solve::svars];\n  (* no relation \
with al = 1, or a one-parameter family of relations (two of the forms are a \
dependent pair, handled by pairRules): no triple rule *)\n  If[sol === {} || \
!FreeQ[{al, be, ga} /. First[sol], al | be | ga], None, With[{c = {al, be, \
ga} /. First[sol]}, {c, Expand[c.L /. {A -> 0, B -> 0}]}]]];\npairRules = \
Table[With[{f1 = pair[[1]], f2 = pair[[2]], c = Expand[forms[pair[[1]]] + \
forms[pair[[2]]]]},\n  f1^a_. f2^b_. /; a < 0 && b < 0 :> f1^(a + 1) f2^(b + \
1) (1/f1 + 1/f2)/c], {pair, {{fA, fAp}, {fB, fBp}, {fC, fCp}}}];\ntripleRules \
= Flatten[Table[With[{r = relation[triple]}, If[r === None || r[[2]] === 0, \
Nothing,\n  With[{f1 = triple[[1]], f2 = triple[[2]], f3 = triple[[3]], c = \
r[[1]], de = r[[2]]},\n    f1^a_. f2^b_. f3^d_. /; a < 0 && b < 0 && d < 0 :> \
f1^(a + 1) f2^(b + 1) f3^(d + 1) (c[[1]]/(f2 f3) + c[[2]]/(f1 f3) + \
c[[3]]/(f1 f2))/de]]],\n  {triple, Subsets[Keys[forms], \
{3}]}]];\nnegativeForms[term_] := Select[Keys[forms], Exponent[term, #] < 0 \
&];\n(* the additive terms of an expression: a single product is one term, \
not a list of its factors; zero has none *)\ntermList[expr_] := With[{e = \
Expand[expr]}, Which[e === 0, {}, Head[e] === Plus, List @@ e, True, \
{e}]];\n(* Partial fractions of a unit propagator monomial. Scalar \
coefficients are\n   spectators and are combined by the shared sparse \
converter. *)\npartialFractionMonomial[expr_] := Module[{e = expr, old},\n  \
(* a numerator power of A (B) over a denominator A' (B') is written through \
A' (B'): the pair is dependent *)\n  e = Expand[e /. {fA^n_. fAp^m_. /; n > 0 \
&& m < 0 :> (-(s + t) - fAp)^n fAp^m, fB^n_. fBp^m_. /; n > 0 && m < 0 :> \
(-(s + u) - fBp)^n fBp^m} /. u -> s4 - s - t];\n  Do[old = e; e = Expand[e \
//. pairRules]; e = Expand[e /. tripleRules]; If[e === old, Break[]], \
{20}];\n  Require[Max[Prepend[Length[negativeForms[#]] & /@ termList[e], 0]] \
<= 2, \"Partial fractions did not terminate\"];\n  Require[Together[(e - \
expr) /. forms] === 0,\n    \"A geometric partial fraction does not \
reconstruct its monomial\", expr];\n  e];\nfractionConverter = \
CreatePartialFractionConverter[Keys[forms], spe3, \
partialFractionMonomial];\nrealFractionResults = Association @ Table[spin -> \
fractionConverter[\n  toForms[algebra[\"Real\"][spin] /. D -> 4 - 2 eps] /. \
numeratorForms], {spin, spins}];\nRequire[FreeQ[realFractionResults, \
_Failure], \"Sparse partial fractions failed\", \
realFractionResults];\nrealFractionTerms = Association @ Table[spin -> \
realFractionResults[spin][\"Terms\"], {spin, spins}];\nrealFractions = Total \
/@ realFractionTerms;   (* the coefficients are rational in eps (the gluon \
average 1/(D-2)) *)\nLength /@ realFractions", "Input"], 
  Cell["Check: the partial fractions reproduce the matrix element when the \
forms are substituted back.", "Text"], Cell["(* exact rational test points: a \
symbolic simplification of the difference of tens of thousands of terms would \
take hours *)\ntestPoints = {{s -> 7, t -> -2, s4 -> 3/2, A -> -5/3, B -> \
-4/7, eps -> 1/5, spe3 -> 2/9}, {s -> 11, t -> -6, s4 -> 2/3, A -> -1/4, B -> \
-9/5, eps -> -3/7, spe3 -> 5/13}};\nDo[Require[Together[((realFractions[spin] \
/. forms) - (algebra[\"Real\"][spin] /. D -> 4 - 2 eps /. u -> s4 - s - t /. \
C -> -s4 - A - B)) /. point] === 0,\n  \"Partial fractions do not add up\", \
{spin, point}], {spin, spins}, {point, testPoints}];\n\"partial fractions \
checked at exact test points\"", "Input"], Cell["Families and Kira targets", 
   "Section"], Cell["Each term, a coefficient times a product of at most two \
forms, is mapped onto a family and its indices.  The exchange k1 <-> k2 turns \
A', B', C' into A, B, C; pairs with one primed form are mapped onto the mixed \
families real_ABp (A with B'), real_ACp (A with C') and real_BCp (B with C'). \
 The coefficients, functions of s, t, s4 only, are not affected.  The symbols \
dm4 = D - 4 and the hatted invariant spe3 are separated: a power spe3^n means \
the integral in D + 2n dimensions times (4 Pi)^n (-1)^n (-eps)_n (the \
lepton-quark notebook derives this).", "Text"], 
  Cell["(* the families and their two forms; the exchange k1 <-> k2 maps \
every form onto its primed partner *)\nfamilyForms = <|KRealAB -> {fA, fB}, \
KRealAC -> {fA, fC}, KRealBC -> {fB, fC}, KRealABp -> {fA, fBp}, KRealACp -> \
{fA, fCp}, KRealBCp -> {fB, fCp}|>;\nswapForms = {fA -> fAp, fAp -> fA, fB -> \
fBp, fBp -> fB, fC -> fCp, fCp -> fC};\nswapInvariants = {A -> -(s + t) - A, \
B -> -(s + u) - B} /. u -> s4 - s - t;         (* k1 <-> k2 on the invariants \
*)\nheadOf[names_List] := Which[names === {} || names === {fA} || names === \
{fB} || Sort[names] === {fA, fB}, KRealAB,\n  names === {fC} || Sort[names] \
=== Sort[{fA, fC}], KRealAC,   Sort[names] === Sort[{fB, fC}], KRealBC,\n  \
Sort[names] === Sort[{fA, fBp}], KRealABp,   Sort[names] === Sort[{fA, fCp}], \
KRealACp,   Sort[names] === Sort[{fB, fCp}], KRealBCp,\n  True, None];\n(* \
family of a term from its denominator forms: with or without the relabelling \
k1 <-> k2 *)\nfamilyOf[denominators_List] := Module[{head = \
headOf[denominators], swap = False},\n  If[head === None, swap = True; head = \
headOf[denominators /. swapForms]];\n  Require[head =!= None, \"Unexpected \
pair of denominator forms\", denominators];\n  {head, swap}];\n(* A and B \
through the two forms X, Y of each family, solved once *)\nfamilySolutions = \
Association @ KeyValueMap[Function[{head, pair}, head -> First[Solve[{X == \
forms[pair[[1]]], Y == forms[pair[[2]]]}, {A, B}]]], \
familyForms];\ntermRows[expr_] := Module[{terms = CombineLaurentTerms[expr, \
Append[Keys[forms], spe3]]},\n  Require[ListQ[terms] && FreeQ[terms, \
_Failure], \"Laurent coefficient grouping failed\", terms];\n  \
Flatten[Table[Module[{den, head, swap, pair, powers, numerator, sol, poly, \
rows},\n    den = negativeForms[term];\n    {head, swap} = familyOf[den];\n   \
 pair = familyForms[head]; sol = familySolutions[head];\n    (* denominator \
powers of the two family forms (after the relabelling, if any) *)\n    powers \
= Association @ Table[(f /. If[swap, swapForms, {}]) -> -Exponent[term, f], \
{f, den}];\n    (* the rest of the term: coefficient times positive powers of \
forms, written in A and B (relabelled with the term) and then in the two \
family forms X, Y *)\n    numerator = term Times @@ Table[f^(-Exponent[term, \
f]), {f, den}] /. forms;\n    If[swap, numerator = numerator /. \
swapInvariants];\n    poly = Expand[numerator /. sol];\n    \
Require[PolynomialQ[poly, {X, Y, spe3}], \"A numerator is not polynomial in \
the family forms\", term];\n    rows = Table[<|\"Integral\" -> head[1, 1, \
Lookup[powers, pair[[1]], 0] - rule[[1, 1]], Lookup[powers, pair[[2]], 0] - \
rule[[1, 2]]],\n      \"Dm4Power\" -> 0, \"HatPower\" -> rule[[1, 3]], \
\"Coefficient\" -> Factor[rule[[2]]]|>, {rule, CoefficientRules[poly, {X, Y, \
spe3}]}];\n    (* check: the rows rebuild the (relabelled) term *)\n    \
Require[Together[(Total[(#[\"Coefficient\"] dm4^#[\"Dm4Power\"] \
spe3^#[\"HatPower\"] X^(-#[\"Integral\"][[3]]) Y^(-#[\"Integral\"][[4]]) & /@ \
rows)] /.\n        {X -> forms[pair[[1]]], Y -> forms[pair[[2]]]}) - (term /. \
forms /. If[swap, swapInvariants, {}])] === 0, \"The rows of a term do not \
rebuild it\", term];\n    rows], {term, terms}]]];\n(* The existing mapper \
above acts on a unit monomial and retains its exact\n   reconstruction test. \
After multiplication by the scalar coefficient, check\n   the full \
contribution again, including any k1 <-> k2 relabelling. \
*)\nreconstructRows[term_, rows_List] := Module[{head, swap, pair, \
rebuilt},\n  {head, swap} = familyOf[negativeForms[term]]; pair = \
familyForms[head];\n  rebuilt = Total[(#[\"Coefficient\"] dm4^#[\"Dm4Power\"] \
spe3^#[\"HatPower\"]\n    forms[pair[[1]]]^(-#[\"Integral\"][[3]]) \
forms[pair[[2]]]^(-#[\"Integral\"][[4]])) & /@ rows];\n  Together[rebuilt - \
(term /. forms /. If[swap, swapInvariants, {}])] === 0];\nrowConverter = \
CreateIntegralRowConverter[Append[Keys[forms], spe3], termRows, \
reconstructRows];\nrealRowResults = Association @ Table[spin -> \
rowConverter[realFractionTerms[spin]], {spin, \
spins}];\nRequire[FreeQ[realRowResults, _Failure], \"Sparse integral-row \
conversion failed\", realRowResults];\nrealTerms = Association @ Table[spin \
-> realRowResults[spin][\"Rows\"], {spin, spins}];\nindexRanges = \
<|\"denominators\" -> Max[Total[Select[List @@ #[\"Integral\"], # > 0 &]] & \
/@ Flatten[Values[realTerms]]],\n  \"numerators\" -> Max[-Total[Select[List \
@@ #[\"Integral\"], # < 0 &]] & /@ \
Flatten[Values[realTerms]]]|>;\nRequire[indexRanges[\"denominators\"] <= 8 && \
indexRanges[\"numerators\"] <= 8, \"The integrals exceed the ranges r = 8, s \
= 8 of kira/real/jobs.yaml\", indexRanges];\nindexRanges", "Input"], 
  Cell[
   "Dataset[realTerms[\"TT\"][[1 ;; Min[8, Length[realTerms[\"TT\"]]]]]]", 
   "Input"], Cell["Reduction with Kira", "Section"], 
  Cell["Real families real_AB ... real_BCp (kira/real) and the one-loop \
families (kira/virtual); Kira sets s = 1, RestoreScale puts it back.  The \
virtual integrals come from step 2 already labelled (KVirtualST etc.).", 
   "Text"], Cell["realHeads = {KRealAB -> \"real_AB\", KRealAC -> \
\"real_AC\", KRealBC -> \"real_BC\", KRealABp -> \"real_ABp\", KRealACp -> \
\"real_ACp\", KRealBCp -> \"real_BCp\"};\nvirtualHeads = {KVirtualST -> \
\"virtual_ST\", KVirtualSU -> \"virtual_SU\", KVirtualTU -> \
\"virtual_TU\"};\nreferenceRealMasters = Join[{KRealAB[1, 1, 0, 0]}, #[1, 1, \
1, 1] & /@ Keys[realHeads]];\nreferenceVirtualMasters = Flatten[Table[head @@ \
indices, {head, Keys[virtualHeads]},\n  {indices, Select[Tuples[{0, 1}, 4], \
MemberQ[{2, 4}, Total[#]] &]}]];\nrealTargets = \
Union[Flatten[Lookup[realTerms[#], \"Integral\"] & /@ spins], \
referenceRealMasters];\nvirtualTargets = Union[Cases[algebra[\"Virtual\"], \
(KVirtualST | KVirtualSU | KVirtualTU)[__], Infinity]];\nresultsDir = \
ResultsDirectory[route <> \"/class-\" <> class];\nkiraReal = \
PrepareKira[FileNameJoin[{NotebookDirectory[], \"kira\", \"real\"}], \
FileNameJoin[{resultsDir, \"kira\", \"real\"}]];\nWriteKiraTargets[kiraReal, \
realTargets, realHeads];\nIf[virtualTargets =!= {},\n  kiraVirtual = \
PrepareKira[FileNameJoin[{NotebookDirectory[], \"kira\", \"virtual\"}], \
FileNameJoin[{resultsDir, \"kira\", \"virtual\"}]];\n  \
WriteKiraTargets[kiraVirtual, virtualTargets, \
virtualHeads]];\n{Length[realTargets], Length[virtualTargets]}", "Input"], 
  Cell["RunKira[kiraReal];\nrealRules = RestoreScale[Join @@ \
Table[KiraRules[kiraReal, name, realHeads], {name, Select[Values[realHeads], \
FileExistsQ[FileNameJoin[{kiraReal, \"results\", #, \"kira_targets.m\"}]] \
&]}],\n  s, {t -> t/s, s4 -> s4/s}, Keys[realHeads]];\nvirtualRules = \
If[virtualTargets === {}, {}, RunKira[kiraVirtual];\n  RestoreScale[Join @@ \
Table[KiraRules[kiraVirtual, name, virtualHeads], {name, \
Select[Values[virtualHeads], FileExistsQ[FileNameJoin[{kiraVirtual, \
\"results\", #, \"kira_targets.m\"}]] &]}],\n    s, {t -> t/s}, \
Keys[virtualHeads]]];\nrealMasters = Union[Cases[realRules[[All, 2]], \
(Alternatives @@ Keys[realHeads])[__], Infinity]];\nvirtualMasters = \
Union[Cases[virtualRules[[All, 2]], (Alternatives @@ Keys[virtualHeads])[__], \
Infinity]];\nCheckReductionCoverage[realTargets, realRules, Keys[realHeads], \
referenceRealMasters];\nCheckReductionCoverage[virtualTargets, virtualRules, \
Keys[virtualHeads], referenceVirtualMasters];\n{realMasters, virtualMasters}"\
, "Input"], Cell["Expected masters: the volume real_AB[1,1,0,0] and the \
angular integrals [1,1,1,1] of each family; for the loop: the bubbles \
[0,1,0,1] (s channel), [0,1,1,0] / [1,0,0,1] type (t, u) and the boxes \
[1,1,1,1].  A term with spe3^n or loopHat2^n uses the rules at d -> 4 + 2n - \
2 eps; KiraMaster[family, indices, 2n] denotes a master in D + 2n dimensions. \
 Hatted terms occur in both projections here (the transverse densities are \
four-dimensional objects inside D-dimensional traces), as in the helicity \
difference of Processes/Hadronic.", "Text"], Cell["label[head_, heads_] := \
head /. heads;\n(* the rows are first grouped by integral and hat power \
(their coefficients added), so that the reduction rules are applied once per \
distinct integral *)\nrealGrouped = Association @ Table[spin -> \
GroupBy[realTerms[spin], {#[\"Integral\"], #[\"HatPower\"]} &, \
Total[#[\"Coefficient\"] (-2 eps)^#[\"Dm4Power\"] & /@ #] &], {spin, \
spins}];\nrealDispatch = Dispatch[realRules];\nrealReduced = Association @ \
Table[spin -> Collect[Total[KeyValueMap[Function[{key, coefficient}, With[{n \
= key[[2]]},\n  coefficient (4 Pi)^n (-1)^n Pochhammer[-eps, n] *\n    \
((key[[1]] /. realDispatch /. d -> 4 + 2 n - 2 eps) /.\n      (head : \
(Alternatives @@ Keys[realHeads]))[indices__] :> KiraMaster[label[head, \
realHeads], {indices}, 2 n])]],\n  realGrouped[spin]]], _KiraMaster, \
Together], {spin, spins}];\n(* the trace was evaluated in D = 4 - 2 eps \
dimensions, and its coefficients keep that D: only the integration dimension \
of a hatted term is shifted\n   (the Kira rules are written in their own \
dimension symbol d, set below to 4 + 2n - 2 eps).  Replacing the trace's D by \
d would shift the coefficients as well and is wrong\n   (Processes/Hadronic \
learnt this on the helicity difference).\n   A power loopHat2^n of the hatted \
loop momentum under the loop integral d^D loop/(i Pi^(D/2)) equals (-1)^n \
(-eps)_n times the integral in D + 2n dimensions\n   (the (D-4)-dimensional \
angular average; the measure d^D k/(2 Pi)^(D-1) of the real emission gives \
the additional (4 Pi)^n), see the introduction *)\nvirtualReduced = \
Association @ Table[spin -> Collect[Expand[Total[Map[Function[term, With[{n = \
Exponent[term, HatPower[_]] /. 0 -> 0},\n  Module[{hat = FirstCase[term, \
HatPower[m_] :> m, 0]},\n    (-1)^hat Pochhammer[-eps, hat] (term /. \
HatPower[_] -> 1 /. D -> 4 - 2 eps /. virtualRules /. d -> 4 + 2 hat - 2 eps) \
/.\n      (head : (Alternatives @@ Keys[virtualHeads]))[indices__] :> \
KiraMaster[label[head, virtualHeads], {indices}, 2 hat]]]],\n  \
If[algebra[\"Virtual\"][spin] === 0, {}, \
termList[algebra[\"Virtual\"][spin]]]]]], _KiraMaster, Together], {spin, \
spins}];\nRequire[FreeQ[{realReduced, virtualReduced}, Alternatives @@ \
Join[Keys[realHeads], Keys[virtualHeads]]], \"Some integrals were not \
reduced\"];\n(* the box masters (four propagators) are evaluated through \
order eps^0 only: their coefficients must be regular at eps = 0 \
*)\nboxMasters = Union[Cases[virtualReduced, m_KiraMaster /; \
StringStartsQ[m[[1]], \"virtual\"] && Count[m[[2]], 1] == 4, \
Infinity]];\nRequire[And @@ \
Flatten[Table[FreeQ[Normal[Series[Coefficient[virtualReduced[spin], m], {eps, \
0, -1}]], eps], {spin, spins}, {m, boxMasters}]],\n  \"A box coefficient has \
a pole at eps = 0: the box masters would be needed beyond order \
eps^0\"];\nUnion[Cases[{realReduced, virtualReduced}, _KiraMaster, \
Infinity]]", "Input"], Cell["Phase-space masters", "Section"], 
  Cell["As in the lepton-quark process: the two-body volume Phi2 (and Phi2' \
in D+2), the angular function Omega(z) with its threshold branch z^(-1-eps) \
separated by the connection formula (F1, F2 inert), and for the mixed \
families the regular function Omega(1-z) = 2(1-2eps) integral_0^Infinity dy \
(1+y)^eps/(1+(1-z)y) (its D+2 analogue with (1+y)^(eps-1) and 2(3-2eps)), \
which is analytic at z = 0 and kept as the inert functions F3, F4.", "Text"], 
  Cell["LoadSubTropica[]", "Input"], Cell["masters = <|\n  \"phaseSpace\" -> \
EulerIntegral[1/Gamma[1 - eps], x^(-eps) (1 + x)^(2 eps - 2), {x}, {}, 2, \
eps],\n  \"phaseSpaceD2\" -> EulerIntegral[1/Gamma[2 - eps], x^(1 - eps) (1 + \
x)^(2 eps - 4), {x}, {}, 1, eps],\n  \"F1\" -> EulerIntegral[1 + eps, (1 + \
y)^(-1 - eps)/(1 + zb y), {y}, {zb}, 2, eps] /. zb -> 1 - z,\n  \"F2\" -> \
EulerIntegral[eps, (1 + y)^(-eps)/(1 + zb y), {y}, {zb}, 2, eps] /. zb -> 1 - \
z,\n  \"F3\" -> EulerIntegral[2 (1 - 2 eps), (1 + y)^eps/(1 + zb y), {y}, \
{zb}, 2, eps] /. zb -> 1 - z,\n  \"F4\" -> EulerIntegral[2 (3 - 2 eps), (1 + \
y)^(eps - 1)/(1 + zb y), {y}, {zb}, 1, eps] /. zb -> 1 - z|>;\ncheck[x_] := \
Require[Simplify[x] === 0, \"Master integral check failed\", \
x];\ncheck[Normal[Series[masters[\"phaseSpace\"] - Gamma[1 - eps]/Gamma[2 - 2 \
eps], {eps, 0, 2}]]];\ncheck[Normal[Series[masters[\"phaseSpaceD2\"] - \
Gamma[2 - eps]/Gamma[4 - 2 eps], {eps, 0, 1}]]];\ntruncationCheck[series_, \
exact_, power_] := Module[{d1, d2},\n  d1 = N[(exact - series) /. {eps -> \
-1/50, z -> 1/3}, 30];\n  d2 = N[(exact - series) /. {eps -> -1/100, z -> \
1/3}, 30];\n  Require[Abs[d2/d1 - 2^-power] < 2^-power/10, \"Master integral \
disagrees with its closed form\", {d1, d2}]; {d1, \
d2}];\ntruncationCheck[masters[\"F1\"], Hypergeometric2F1[1, 1, 2 + eps, z], \
3];\ntruncationCheck[masters[\"F2\"], Hypergeometric2F1[1, 1, 1 + eps, z], \
3];\ntruncationCheck[masters[\"F3\"], -2 (1 - 2 eps)/eps Hypergeometric2F1[1, \
1, 1 - eps, z], 3];\ntruncationCheck[masters[\"F4\"], 2 (3 - 2 eps)/(1 - eps) \
Hypergeometric2F1[1, 1, 2 - eps, z], 2]", "Input"], 
  Cell["angular[zz_] := -2 (1 - 2 eps)/eps (Gamma[1 - eps] Gamma[1 + eps] (1 \
- zz)^eps zz^(-1 - eps) +\n  Gamma[1 - eps] Gamma[-1 - eps]/Gamma[-eps]^2 \
Sum[eps^n F1[n][zz], {n, 0, 2}]);\nangularD2[zz_] := 2 (3 - 2 eps)/(1 - eps) \
(Gamma[2 - eps] Gamma[eps] (1 - zz)^(eps - 1) zz^(-eps) +\n  Gamma[2 - eps] \
Gamma[-eps]/Gamma[1 - eps]^2 Sum[eps^n F2[n][zz], {n, 0, \
2}]);\nangularMixed[zz_] := Sum[eps^n F3[n][zz], {n, -1, 2}];                 \
(* Omega(1-z): regular at z = 0 *)\nangularMixedD2[zz_] := Sum[eps^n \
F4[n][zz], {n, 0, 1}];\n(* at the threshold the mixed masters are elementary: \
Omega(1 - z) at z = 0 is 2 (1-2eps) B(-eps, 1) = -2/eps + 4, and the D+2 one \
2 (3-2eps) B(1-eps, 1) = 2 (3-2eps)/(1-eps);\n   the explicit functions are \
regular at z = 0 and must reproduce these values (checked below) \
*)\nthresholdValues = Join[Table[F3[n][0] -> SeriesCoefficient[-2 (1 - 2 \
eps)/eps, {eps, 0, n}], {n, -1, 2}], Table[F4[n][0] -> SeriesCoefficient[2 (3 \
- 2 eps)/(1 - eps), {eps, 0, n}], {n, 0, 1}]];\nthresholdValues = \
Join[{F1[0][0] -> 1, F2[0][0] -> 1, F1[_][0] -> 0, F2[_][0] -> 0}, \
thresholdValues];   (* 2F1(1,1;c;0) = 1 for the unmixed masters \
*)\nmasterFunctions = Join[thresholdValues,\n  Table[F1[n][zz_] :> \
Evaluate[SeriesCoefficient[masters[\"F1\"], {eps, 0, n}] /. z -> zz], {n, 0, \
2}],\n  Table[F2[n][zz_] :> Evaluate[SeriesCoefficient[masters[\"F2\"], {eps, \
0, n}] /. z -> zz], {n, 0, 2}],\n  Table[F3[n][zz_] :> \
Evaluate[SeriesCoefficient[masters[\"F3\"], {eps, 0, n}] /. z -> zz], {n, -1, \
2}],\n  Table[F4[n][zz_] :> Evaluate[SeriesCoefficient[masters[\"F4\"], {eps, \
0, n}] /. z -> zz], {n, 0, 1}]];\nnumericCheck[expr_, integrand_, power_] := \
Module[{d1, d2},\n  d1 = N[expr /. {eps -> -1/40, z -> 1/3}, 20] - \
NIntegrate[integrand /. {eps -> -1/40, z -> 1/3}, {x, 0, Infinity}, \
WorkingPrecision -> 30];\n  d2 = N[expr /. {eps -> -1/80, z -> 1/3}, 20] - \
NIntegrate[integrand /. {eps -> -1/80, z -> 1/3}, {x, 0, Infinity}, \
WorkingPrecision -> 30];\n  Require[Abs[d2/d1 - 2^-power] < 2^-power/10, \
\"Angular master disagrees with direct integration\", {d1, d2}]; {d1, \
d2}];\nRequire[And @@ Table[Simplify[Limit[F3[n][z] /. masterFunctions, z -> \
0] - (F3[n][0] /. thresholdValues)] === 0, {n, -1, 2}] &&\n  And @@ \
Table[Simplify[Limit[F4[n][z] /. masterFunctions, z -> 0] - (F4[n][0] /. \
thresholdValues)] === 0, {n, 0, 1}], \"The mixed masters do not reach their \
threshold values\"];\nnumericCheck[angular[z] /. masterFunctions, 2 (1 - 2 \
eps) x^(-1 - eps) (1 + x)^eps/(z + x), 3];\nnumericCheck[angularD2[z] /. \
masterFunctions, 2 (3 - 2 eps) x^(-eps) (1 + x)^(eps - 1)/(z + x), \
2];\nnumericCheck[angularMixed[z] /. masterFunctions, 2 (1 - 2 eps) x^(-1 - \
eps) (1 + x)^eps/(1 - z + x), 3];\nnumericCheck[angularMixedD2[z] /. \
masterFunctions, 2 (3 - 2 eps) x^(-eps) (1 + x)^(eps - 1)/(1 - z + x), 2]", 
   "Input"], Cell["The physical masters.  Phi2 = (4 Pi)^eps s4^(-eps)/(8 Pi) \
Gamma(1-eps)/Gamma(2-2eps), Phi2' = (4 Pi)^(eps-1) s4^(1-eps)/(8 Pi) \
Gamma(2-eps)/Gamma(4-2eps); the angular masters with the cross ratios of the \
pairs (pa, pb), (pa, p), (pb, p),\n\n   zAB = s s4/((s+t)(s+u)),   zAC = -t \
s4/((s+t)(s-s4)),   zBC = -u s4/((s+u)(s-s4)),   (2 pa.pRec = s+t, 2 pb.pRec \
= s+u, 2 p.pRec = s-s4),\n\nand the normalization sigma sigma' Phi2 \
Omega(z)/((2 q.pRec)(2 q'.pRec)) explained in the introduction.  The \
lepton-quark process checked this formula for the unmixed pairs against its \
literature result; the mixed one is checked here by a direct numerical \
angular integration in D = 4 - 2 eps dimensions at eps = -1/3 (the angular \
measure of the recoil rest frame is sin^(1-2eps)theta1 dtheta1 \
sin^(-2eps)theta2 dtheta2), against the exact Euler integral of Omega(1 - \
zAB).", "Text"], Cell["twoPRec = <|pa -> s + t, pb -> s + u, p -> s - \
s4|>;\nsign = <|pa -> -1, pb -> -1, p -> 1|>;\ncrossRatio[q_, qp_] := s4 (2 \
ScalarProductValue[q, qp])/(twoPRec[q] twoPRec[qp]);        (* z = s4 \
(q.q')/(2 (q.pRec)(q'.pRec)) with twoPRec = 2 q.pRec \
*)\nScalarProductValue[pa, pb] = s/2; ScalarProductValue[pa, p] = -t/2; \
ScalarProductValue[pb, p] = -u/2;\nzAB = Simplify[crossRatio[pa, pb]]; zAC = \
Simplify[crossRatio[pa, p]]; zBC = Simplify[crossRatio[pb, \
p]];\nRequire[Simplify[{zAB - s s4/((s + t) (s + u)), zAC + t s4/((s + t) (s \
- s4)), zBC + u s4/((s + u) (s - s4))}] === {0, 0, 0}, \"cross \
ratios\"];\nphaseSpace = (4 Pi)^eps s4^(-eps)/(8 Pi) \
masters[\"phaseSpace\"];\nphaseSpaceD2 = (4 Pi)^(eps - 1) s4^(1 - eps)/(8 Pi) \
masters[\"phaseSpaceD2\"];\npairs = <|\"real_AB\" -> {pa, pb, zAB, False}, \
\"real_AC\" -> {pa, p, zAC, False}, \"real_BC\" -> {pb, p, zBC, False},\n  \
\"real_ABp\" -> {pa, pb, zAB, True}, \"real_ACp\" -> {pa, p, zAC, True}, \
\"real_BCp\" -> {pb, p, zBC, True}|>;\nphysicalMasters = \
Join[{KiraMaster[\"real_AB\", {1, 1, 0, 0}, 0] -> phaseSpace, \
KiraMaster[\"real_AB\", {1, 1, 0, 0}, 2] -> phaseSpaceD2},\n  \
Flatten[Table[With[{q = pairs[name][[1]], qp = pairs[name][[2]], zz = \
pairs[name][[3]], mixed = pairs[name][[4]]},\n    {KiraMaster[name, {1, 1, 1, \
1}, 0] -> sign[q] sign[qp] phaseSpace If[mixed, angularMixed[zz], \
angular[zz]]/(twoPRec[q] twoPRec[qp]),\n     KiraMaster[name, {1, 1, 1, 1}, \
2] -> sign[q] sign[qp] phaseSpaceD2 If[mixed, angularMixedD2[zz], \
angularD2[zz]]/(twoPRec[q] twoPRec[qp])}],\n    {name, \
Keys[pairs]}]]];\nLength[physicalMasters]", "Input"], 
  Cell["(* numerical check of the mixed-family master formula: integral over \
the two-body phase space of 1/(A B') at eps = -1/3, s = 1, t = -3/10, s4 = \
1/5 *)\nmixedCheck = Module[{epsValue = -1/3, sv = 1, tv = -3/10, s4v = 1/5, \
uv, Ea, Eb, Ep, ca, cb, cp, direct, formula, measure, k1, integrate},\n  uv = \
s4v - sv - tv;\n  (* recoil rest frame: pRec = (Sqrt[s4], 0); external \
momenta from the invariants, p along z, pa and pb in the plane phi = 0 and \
phi = phi_b *)\n  Ea = (sv + tv)/(2 Sqrt[s4v]); Eb = (sv + uv)/(2 Sqrt[s4v]); \
Ep = (sv - s4v)/(2 Sqrt[s4v]);\n  cp = {0, 0, 1};\n  ca = Module[{c = 1 - \
(-tv/2)/(Ea Ep)}, {Sqrt[1 - c^2], 0, c}];\n  cb = Module[{c = 1 - (-uv/2)/(Eb \
Ep), cab, x}, cab = 1 - (sv/2)/(Ea Eb);      (* cab = ca.cb from pa.pb = s/2 \
*)\n    x = (cab - ca[[3]] c)/ca[[1]];                                        \
      (* the x component of cb; the y component follows from |cb| = 1 *)\n    \
{x, Sqrt[1 - c^2 - x^2], c}];\n  k1[th1_, th2_] := {Sin[th1] Cos[th2], \
Sin[th1] Sin[th2], Cos[th1]};\n  (* angular measure in D - 1 = 3 - 2 eps \
space dimensions; the integrand 1/(A B') has integrable singularities where \
k1 is parallel to pa or pb,\n     which NIntegrate handles with its \
convergence warnings suppressed; the comparison tolerance is 10^-3 *)\n  \
integrate[f_] := Quiet[NIntegrate[f, {th1, 0, Pi}, {th2, 0, Pi}, \
WorkingPrecision -> 20, PrecisionGoal -> 6, MaxRecursion -> 30], \
{NIntegrate::ncvb, NIntegrate::slwcon}];\n  measure = integrate[Sin[th1]^(1 - \
2 epsValue) Sin[th2]^(-2 epsValue)];\n  (* 1/(A B') with A = -2 pa.k1 = \
-(s+t)(1 - ca.n)/2, B' = -2 pb.k2 = -(s+u)(1 + cb.n)/2 in the recoil frame \
*)\n  direct = integrate[Sin[th1]^(1 - 2 epsValue) Sin[th2]^(-2 \
epsValue)/((-(sv + tv) (1 - ca.k1[th1, th2])/2) (-(sv + uv) (1 + cb.k1[th1, \
th2])/2))]/measure;\n  (* the master Omega(1 - zAB) as its exact Euler \
integral (the eps series of F3 is truncated and would be off by a few percent \
at eps = -1/3) *)\n  formula = With[{zv = zAB /. {s -> sv, t -> tv, u -> uv, \
s4 -> s4v}},\n    N[sign[pa] sign[pb]/(twoPRec[pa] twoPRec[pb]) /. {s -> sv, \
t -> tv, u -> uv, s4 -> s4v}, 20] *\n      NIntegrate[2 (1 - 2 epsValue) \
x^(-1 - epsValue) (1 + x)^epsValue/(1 - zv + x), {x, 0, Infinity}, \
WorkingPrecision -> 20]];\n  {direct, \
formula}];\nRequire[Abs[mixedCheck[[1]]/mixedCheck[[2]] - 1] < 10^-3, \"The \
mixed-family angular master formula fails its numerical check\", \
mixedCheck];\nmixedCheck", "Input"], Cell["Loop masters", "Section"], 
  Cell["With the measure d^D loop/(i Pi^(D/2)) the massless bubble with \
external momentum squared P^2 < 0 is (-P^2)^(-eps) Gamma(eps) \
Gamma(1-eps)^2/Gamma(2-2eps) (Euler integral as in the lepton-quark process), \
and the massless box with invariants S, T < 0 has the Feynman-parameter \
representation (Cheng-Wu: x4 = 1)\n\n   Box(S,T) = Gamma(2+eps) integral dx1 \
dx2 dx3 (1 + x1 + x2 + x3)^(2 eps) (-S x1 x3 - T x2)^(-2-eps),\n\nevaluated \
by SubTropica as a series in eps for -S = 1 (the scale is restored by \
dimensional analysis, Box ~ S^(-2-eps)) and -T/-S = r.  In the physical \
region s > 0 the invariants become s -> s + i0 (the Feynman prescription); \
the real parts of the continued masters enter the cross section: (-s)^(-eps) \
-> s^(-eps) cos(Pi eps), log(-s) -> log(s) - i Pi inside the logarithms of \
the box, whose real part is checked against the standard formula Re Box(s,t) \
= (2 rGamma/(s t)) [ (s^(-eps) cos(Pi eps) + (-t)^(-eps))/eps^2 - \
log^2(s/(-t))/2 ] + O(eps) with rGamma = Gamma(1+eps) \
Gamma(1-eps)^2/Gamma(1-2eps).  The boxes in D+2 (needed for the hatted loop \
momentum) are finite and evaluated the same way.", "Text"], 
  Cell["loopMasters = <|\n  \"bubble\" -> EulerIntegral[Gamma[eps], x^(-eps) \
(1 + x)^(2 eps - 2), {x}, {}, 2, eps],\n  \"bubbleD2\" -> \
EulerIntegral[Gamma[eps - 1], x^(1 - eps) (1 + x)^(2 eps - 4), {x}, {}, 2, \
eps]|>;\n(* SubTropica writes one constant of the order-eps^2 term as the \
multiple polylogarithm Mpl[{1,2},{1,1}] = Li_{1,2}(1,1) = Sum_{0<k1<k2} 1/(k1 \
k2^2) = zeta(2,1), which equals zeta(3) by Euler's identity \
*)\nmultiplePolylogValues = {HyperIntica`Mpl[{1, 2}, {1, 1}] -> \
Zeta[3]};\nloopMasters = loopMasters /. \
multiplePolylogValues;\nRequire[FreeQ[loopMasters, HyperIntica`Mpl], \"An \
unevaluated multiple polylogarithm remains in a loop master\", \
Cases[loopMasters, _HyperIntica`Mpl, Infinity]];\n(* Quiet: the order-eps^2 \
coefficient contains PolyGamma[2, 1] + 2 Zeta[3], which is zero but which \
Series cannot decide (Series::ztest1); FullSimplify in check[] does \
*)\ncheck[FullSimplify[Quiet[Normal[Series[loopMasters[\"bubble\"] - \
Gamma[eps] Gamma[1 - eps]^2/Gamma[2 - 2 eps], {eps, 0, 2}]], \
Series::ztest1]]];\ncheck[FullSimplify[Quiet[Normal[Series[loopMasters[\"bubb\
leD2\"] - Gamma[eps - 1] Gamma[2 - eps]^2/Gamma[4 - 2 eps], {eps, 0, 2}]], \
Series::ztest1]]];\n(* The boxes are needed through order eps^0 only: the \
reduction coefficients of the box masters are regular at d = 4 (checked \
below), unlike those of\n   the bubbles.  SubTropica writes the Euclidean box \
(r > 0) with Log[-r], Log[1/r] and PolyLog[2, 1 + r], whose imaginary parts \
cancel: they are\n   rewritten through Log[r], Log[1 + r] and PolyLog[2, -r] \
(Li2(1+r) = Pi^2/6 - Li2(-r) - Log[1+r] Log[-r], Log[-r] = Log[r] + I Pi \
sigma with the\n   branch sigma = +1 or -1 of SubTropica's continuation, \
whichever makes the result real), and the real result is kept. \
*)\nrealEuclidean[expr_] := Module[{candidates, real},\n  candidates = \
Table[Expand[expr /. PolyLog[2, 1 + r] -> Pi^2/6 - PolyLog[2, -r] - Log[1 + \
r] (Log[r] + I Pi sigma) /. {Log[-r] -> Log[r] + I Pi sigma, Log[1/r] -> \
-Log[r]}], {sigma, {1, -1}}];\n  imaginaryPart[e_] := Simplify[(e - (e /. \
Complex[x_, y_] :> Complex[x, -y]))/(2 I)];\n  real = Select[candidates, \
imaginaryPart[#] === 0 &];\n  Require[real =!= {}, \"The Euclidean box is not \
real for either branch\", candidates];\n  Collect[(First[real] + (First[real] \
/. Complex[x_, y_] :> Complex[x, -y]))/2, eps, Simplify]];\n(* Quiet: the \
series expansion inside EulerIntegral cannot decide the sign of combinations \
of Log[-r], Log[1/r] and Log[r] that vanish for r > 0 (Series::ztest1); \
realEuclidean resolves them *)\nboxEuclid = \
realEuclidean[Quiet[EulerIntegral[Gamma[2 + eps], (1 + x1 + x2 + x3)^(2 eps) \
(x1 x3 + r x2)^(-2 - eps), {x1, x2, x3}, {r}, 0, eps], Series::ztest1]]", 
   "Input"], Cell["boxD2Euclid = realEuclidean[Quiet[EulerIntegral[Gamma[1 + \
eps], (1 + x1 + x2 + x3)^(2 eps - 2) (x1 x3 + r x2)^(-1 - eps), {x1, x2, x3}, \
{r}, 0, eps], Series::ztest1]]", "Input"], Cell["Check of the Euclidean box \
against the literature expansion (Bern, Dixon and Kosower; here S = -1, r = \
T/S): Box = (2 rGamma/(S T)) [ ((-S)^(-eps) + (-T)^(-eps))/eps^2 - \
log^2(S/T)/2 - Pi^2/2 ] + O(eps); the finite D+2 box is checked numerically \
against its Feynman-parameter integral at eps = 0.", "Text"], 
  Cell["boxLiterature = 2 Gamma[1 + eps] Gamma[1 - eps]^2/Gamma[1 - 2 eps]/r \
((1 + r^(-eps))/eps^2 - Log[1/r]^2/2 - \
Pi^2/2);\ncheck[Simplify[Normal[Series[boxEuclid - boxLiterature, {eps, 0, \
0}]], r > 0]];\n(* numerical check of the D+2 box, which is finite: at eps = \
0 its order-eps^0 value is exact and is compared with the Feynman-parameter \
integral\n   itself (the four-dimensional box has infrared poles, and its \
Feynman-parameter integral converges only for eps well below zero, where \
the\n   truncated series is useless; it is checked against the literature \
above) *)\nboxNumericCheck = Module[{rv = 3/7, direct, series},\n  (* the \
integrand is singular at the origin (integrable); NIntegrate reaches 10^-7 \
but warns about its error estimate, which is suppressed *)\n  direct = \
Quiet[NIntegrate[(1 + x1 + x2 + x3)^(-2) (x1 x3 + rv x2)^(-1), {x1, 0, \
Infinity}, {x2, 0, Infinity}, {x3, 0, Infinity},\n    WorkingPrecision -> 20, \
PrecisionGoal -> 10, MaxRecursion -> 30], {NIntegrate::eincr, \
NIntegrate::slwcon}];\n  series = N[boxD2Euclid /. {eps -> 0, r -> rv}, \
20];\n  Require[Abs[direct/series - 1] < 10^-6, \"The D+2 box disagrees with \
its Feynman-parameter integral\", {direct, series}]; {direct, \
series}];\nboxNumericCheck", "Input"], Cell["Continuation to the physical \
region.  The reduced virtual amplitude contains, after the ordinary \
reduction, the bubbles in s, t, u and the boxes in (s,t), (s,u), (t,u) (and \
their D+2 versions).  With t, u < 0 only the s-channel objects are continued: \
(-s)^(-eps) -> s^(-eps) e^(i Pi eps), i.e. Re = s^(-eps) cos(Pi eps); for the \
boxes, the Euclidean series (a function of logs and dilogarithms of r = T/S) \
is written in terms of log(-S), log(-T) and polylogarithms with arguments \
that stay away from their cuts, and log(-s) -> log(s) - i Pi is applied; the \
real part is taken.  The (s,t) and (s,u) boxes: Box(s,t) = s^(-2-eps) x \
Box(S=-1, r = t/s) ... with the explicit scaling Box(S,T) = (-S)^(-2-eps) \
Box(-1, T/S); the (t,u) box has no continuation.", "Text"], 
  Cell["(* the scaled masters: a one-loop integral with mass dimension -2-eps \
(box) or -eps (bubble) *)\nbubbleOf[P2_] := (-P2)^(-eps) \
loopMasters[\"bubble\"];\nbubbleD2Of[P2_] := (-P2)^(1 - eps) \
loopMasters[\"bubbleD2\"];\nboxOf[S_, T_] := (-S)^(-2 - eps) (boxEuclid /. r \
-> T/S);\nboxD2Of[S_, T_] := (-S)^(-eps) (boxD2Euclid /. r -> T/S);\n(* \
continuation s -> s e^(i Pi) in the physical region (t, u < 0): applied to \
every function of -s, then the real part *)\ncontinue[expr_] := Module[{e = \
expr}, \n  e = e /. (-s)^a_ :> s^a Exp[I Pi a];\n  e = e /. Log[(-s)] -> \
Log[s] - I Pi /. Log[-s] -> Log[s] - I Pi;\n  e = e /. Log[t/s] -> Log[-t/s] \
+ I Pi /. Log[u/s] -> Log[-u/s] + I Pi /. Log[s/t] -> Log[-s/t] - I Pi /. \
Log[s/u] -> Log[-s/u] - I Pi;\n  e];\nrealPart[expr_] := \
ComplexExpand[Re[expr], TargetFunctions -> {Re, Im}] /. Im[_] -> 0 /. Re[x_] \
:> x;", "Input"], Cell["Identification of the loop masters that Kira returns: \
a master with two propagators is the bubble of the momentum difference of the \
two (s, t or u channel), one with all four is the box of its family; the \
invariants of the family's box are S = (q3 - q1)^2 and T = (q4 - q2)^2 for \
the propagator momenta q1 ... q4 (the Feynman-parameter representation above \
has F = -S x1 x3 - T x2 x4).  Triangles do not survive the reduction \
(massless, they are combinations of bubbles) and would be reported.", 
   "Text"], Cell["virtualPropagators = <|\"virtual_ST\" -> {loop, loop + pa, \
loop + pa + pb, loop + p}, \"virtual_SU\" -> {loop, loop + pa, loop + pa + \
pb, loop + pa + pb - p},\n  \"virtual_TU\" -> {loop, loop + pa, loop + pa - \
p, loop + pa - p + pb}|>;\ninvariant[q_] := \
Simplify[ExpandScalarProductRules[q]];\nExpandScalarProductRules[q_] := \
Module[{e = Expand[q]}, (* (q)^2 for q a combination of pa, pb, p *)\n  \
Expand[e^2] /. {pa^2 -> 0, pb^2 -> 0, p^2 -> 0, pa pb -> s/2, pa p -> -t/2, \
pb p -> -u/2, loop -> 0} /. u -> -s - \
t];\nloopMasterValue[KiraMaster[family_, indices_, shift_]] := Module[{q = \
virtualPropagators[family], present, P2, S, T},\n  present = \
Position[indices, 1][[All, 1]];\n  Which[\n    Length[present] == 2 && \
Count[indices, 0] == 2,\n      P2 = invariant[q[[present[[1]]]] - \
q[[present[[2]]]]];\n      Require[P2 =!= 0, \"A scaleless bubble appeared as \
a master\", {family, indices}];\n      If[shift == 0, bubbleOf[P2], \
bubbleD2Of[P2]],\n    indices === {1, 1, 1, 1},\n      S = invariant[q[[3]] - \
q[[1]]]; T = invariant[q[[4]] - q[[2]]];\n      If[shift == 0, boxOf[S, T], \
boxD2Of[S, T]],\n    True, Require[False, \"Unexpected loop master\", \
{family, indices}]]];\nloopMasterRules = Table[m -> loopMasterValue[m], {m, \
Union[Cases[virtualReduced, KiraMaster[f_, __] /; StringStartsQ[f, \
\"virtual\"], Infinity]]}];\nColumn[loopMasterRules /. (a_ -> b_) :> a -> \
Short[b, 3]]", "Input"], Cell["Continuation of the s-channel objects to s > 0 \
and the real part.  The (s,t) and (s,u) boxes are written as (-s)^(-2-eps) \
times the Euclidean function of r = T/S = (-t)/(-s) (or (-u)/(-s)); with s -> \
s e^(-i Pi) (Feynman prescription s + i0, i.e. -s -> s e^(-i Pi)) the \
variable r goes to rp e^(i Pi) with rp = -t/s in (0,1).  The rules below \
continue the functions that occur in the SubTropica result; an unknown \
function stops the notebook.  Then the real part is taken with ComplexExpand \
(eps is real).", "Text"], Cell["boxFunctions = Union[Cases[{boxEuclid, \
boxD2Euclid}, (Log | PolyLog)[___], Infinity]]", "Input"], 
  Cell["continueBox[expr_, rp_] := Module[{e = expr},\n  e = e /. {Log[r] -> \
Log[rp] + I Pi, Log[1 + r] -> Log[1 - rp], PolyLog[2, -r] -> PolyLog[2, rp], \
PolyLog[2, 1 + r] :> (Pi^2/6 - Log[rp] Log[1 - rp] - PolyLog[2, 1 - rp] + I \
Pi Log[1 - rp] /. Log[rp] -> Log[rp] + I Pi)};\n  Require[FreeQ[Cases[e, (Log \
| PolyLog)[___], Infinity], r], \"A function of the box was not continued\", \
Cases[e, (Log | PolyLog)[___], Infinity]];\n  e = e /. r -> -rp;              \
   (* the rational coefficients: r = T/S = -rp *)\n  e];\n(* every master is \
rebuilt with its continuation *)\ncontinued[KiraMaster[family_, indices_, \
shift_]] := Module[{q = virtualPropagators[family], present, P2, S, T, box, \
rp},\n  present = Position[indices, 1][[All, 1]];\n  Which[\n    \
Length[present] == 2,\n      P2 = invariant[q[[present[[1]]]] - \
q[[present[[2]]]]];\n      If[P2 === s, (* s channel: (-s)^(-eps) -> s^(-eps) \
cos(Pi eps) *) \n        If[shift == 0, s^(-eps) Cos[Pi eps] \
loopMasters[\"bubble\"], -s^(1 - eps) Cos[Pi eps] \
loopMasters[\"bubbleD2\"]],\n        If[shift == 0, bubbleOf[P2], \
bubbleD2Of[P2]]],\n    indices === {1, 1, 1, 1},\n      S = invariant[q[[3]] \
- q[[1]]]; T = invariant[q[[4]] - q[[2]]];\n      If[S === s || T === s,\n    \
    (* arrange S as the s channel *)\n        If[T === s, {S, T} = {T, S}];\n \
       rp = -T/s;\n        box = If[shift == 0, boxEuclid, boxD2Euclid];\n    \
    realPart[Exp[-I Pi (If[shift == 0, -2 - eps, -eps])] s^(If[shift == 0, -2 \
- eps, -eps]) continueBox[box, rp]],\n        If[shift == 0, boxOf[S, T], \
boxD2Of[S, T]]]]];\nphysicalLoopMasters = Table[m -> continued[m], {m, \
loopMasterRules[[All, 1]]}];\nColumn[physicalLoopMasters /. (a_ -> b_) :> a \
-> Short[b, 3]]", "Input"], Cell["Check of the continued (s,t) box against \
the literature: Re Box(s,t) = (2 rGamma/(s t)) [ (s^(-eps) cos(Pi eps) + \
(-t)^(-eps))/eps^2 - log^2(s/(-t))/2 ] + O(eps).", "Text"], 
  Cell["boxSTphysical = continued[KiraMaster[\"virtual_ST\", {1, 1, 1, 1}, \
0]];\nboxSTliterature = 2 Gamma[1 + eps] Gamma[1 - eps]^2/Gamma[1 - 2 eps]/(s \
t) ((s^(-eps) Cos[Pi eps] + (-t)^(-eps))/eps^2 - \
Log[s/(-t)]^2/2);\nRequire[Simplify[Normal[Series[boxSTphysical - \
boxSTliterature, {eps, 0, 0}]], s > 0 && t < 0 && t > -s] === 0, \"The \
continued box differs from the literature formula\"];\n\"box continuation \
checked\"", "Input"], Cell["Insert the physical masters and save", 
   "Section"], Cell["realIntegrated = Association @ Table[spin -> \
(realReduced[spin] /. physicalMasters), {spin, spins}];\nvirtualIntegrated = \
Association @ Table[spin -> (virtualReduced[spin] /. physicalLoopMasters), \
{spin, spins}];\nRequire[FreeQ[{realIntegrated, virtualIntegrated}, \
KiraMaster], \"A master integral was not inserted\"];\nreduced = <|\"Real\" \
-> realIntegrated, \"Virtual\" -> virtualIntegrated, \"Masters\" -> masters, \
\"LoopMasters\" -> loopMasters,\n  \"MasterFunctions\" -> masterFunctions, \
\"ThresholdValues\" -> thresholdValues, \"RealRules\" -> realRules, \
\"VirtualRules\" -> virtualRules, \"Route\" -> route, \"Class\" -> \
class|>;\nSaveResult[\"ReductionMetrics\", <|\n  \"ContributionRows\" -> \
Map[Length, realTerms],\n  \"UniqueRealTargets\" -> Length[realTargets], \
\"UniqueVirtualTargets\" -> Length[virtualTargets],\n  \
\"RealMastersIncludingShift\" -> Length[Union[Cases[realReduced, _KiraMaster, \
Infinity]]],\n  \"VirtualMastersIncludingShift\" -> \
Length[Union[Cases[virtualReduced, _KiraMaster, Infinity]]],\n  \
\"SubTropicaSeconds\" -> Total[Lookup[$SubTropicaTimings, \"Seconds\", 0]]|>, \
route <> \"/class-\" <> class];\nSaveResult[\"Reduced\", reduced, route <> \
\"/class-\" <> class];\nKeys[reduced]", "Input"]}, WindowSize -> {1000, 800}]
